// Message passing in the release-acquire fragment -- negative control.
//
// rmm-zoo edge: the control that makes the RA / SRA / WRA splits meaningful.
// Source: Lahav, Giannarakis & Vafeiadis, "Taming Release-Acquire Consistency"
//         (POPL 2016).
//         Vendored shape: rmm-zoo litmus/strictly-weaker/SRA-vs-RA/MP+relacq.
//
// The acquire read of the flag synchronises with the release write, so W(x,1)
// happens-before the read of x; reading x = 0 then reads an mo-earlier write
// while aware of an mo-later one, which read-coherence forbids in WRA, RA and
// SRA alike. A model that allowed this would not be constraining anything and
// the 2+2W split above would be meaningless.
//
// Reference verdicts: WRA, RA, SRA, C11, RC11 and SC all FORBID.
x := 0;
f := 0;
{
  x.store(1, rel);
  f.store(1, rel)
} ||| {
  r0 := f.load(acq);
  r1 := x.load(acq)
}
%%
forbid (r0 = 1 && r1 = 0) [RA]
